00:27:34.260 --> 00:27:40.620
So, in this case, they probably put out a call for, like, two attractive women of a certain age,
所以，在这种情况下，他们可能发布了一个招募通知，比如，需要两名特定年龄的有吸引力的女性，

620
00:27:40.620 --> 00:27:44.060
and then a bunch of photos will get sent into the production,
然后一堆照片会被发送到制作组，

621
00:27:44.060 --> 00:27:47.240
and then they'll sort of pick people based on their photograph.
然后他们会根据照片挑选人选。

622
00:27:47.660 --> 00:27:50.000
Yes, because these are non-speaking roles.
是的，因为这些是非台词角色。

623
00:27:50.560 --> 00:27:54.040
They're background actors, so they didn't need to come in and audition,
他们是背景演员，所以他们不需要过来试镜，

624
00:27:54.300 --> 00:27:57.500
but they would have had their photos looked at to see if they were the right fit.
但他们的照片会被查看，以确定他们是否合适。

625
00:27:57.500 --> 00:27:58.140
Yes.
是的。

626
00:27:58.420 --> 00:28:00.480
And so, similarly, like, a couple weeks ago,
同样地，就像几周前，

627
00:28:00.640 --> 00:28:03.360
when they were making the pyramid in the conference room,
当他们在会议室里搭金字塔时，

628
00:28:03.660 --> 00:28:08.760
they put out a call for background actors who were willing to get into a human pyramid.
他们发布了一个招募通知，寻找愿意参与叠罗汉的背景演员。

629
00:28:08.960 --> 00:28:09.180
Yeah.
是的。

630
00:28:09.580 --> 00:28:09.920
You know?
你知道吗？

631
00:28:10.100 --> 00:28:14.740
And there are agencies that you sign up for if you want to be a background performer.
如果你想成为一名背景表演者，有一些机构可以报名。

632
00:28:14.960 --> 00:28:16.020
And we both did that.
我们俩都做过。

633
00:28:16.160 --> 00:28:17.540
Yes, I did it for many years.
是的，我做了很多年。

634
00:28:17.720 --> 00:28:20.780
I learned a lot about what it was like to be on a set.
我学到了很多关于在片场是什么样的知识。

635
00:28:21.160 --> 00:28:21.600
Yeah.
是的。

636
00:28:21.780 --> 00:28:23.240
It's such great experience.
这是非常棒的经历。

637
00:28:23.420 --> 00:28:24.500
It's a great education.
这是一次很棒的教育。

638
00:28:24.500 --> 00:28:24.880
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

639
00:28:25.460 --> 00:28:28.160
We're now going to shift over to Dunder Mifflin.
我们现在要转到邓德·米夫林公司。

640
00:28:28.580 --> 00:28:29.920
Andy addresses the bullpen.
安迪向办公区发表讲话。

641
00:28:30.060 --> 00:28:32.260
He said, it's time to put their pencils down.
他说，是时候放下铅笔了。

642
00:28:32.380 --> 00:28:33.200
The workday is done.
工作日结束了。

643
00:28:33.320 --> 00:28:37.240
But, hey, also lift them back up because it's the late-night work jam.
但是，嘿，也要把它们重新拿起来，因为这是深夜工作狂欢。

644
00:28:37.740 --> 00:28:38.040
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

645
00:28:38.540 --> 00:28:41.220
Andy and Pam are really trying to get everyone fired up.
安迪和帕姆真的在努力调动大家的积极性。

646
00:28:41.360 --> 00:28:43.060
They're, you know, doing this chant,
你知道，他们正在喊这个口号，

647
00:28:43.160 --> 00:28:44.240
I'm good to go!
我准备好了！

648
00:28:44.620 --> 00:28:47.800
In the background, Angela goes, stop it.
在背景里，安吉拉说，住手。

649
00:28:48.100 --> 00:28:48.700
Stop it.
住手。

650
00:28:54.660 --> 00:28:57.340
I really love Kelly's sweater in this episode.
我真的很喜欢这一集里凯莉穿的毛衣。

651
00:28:57.800 --> 00:29:03.460
It is this sort of gold-yellow color that I'm currently obsessed with.
我现在特别迷恋这种金黄色。

652
00:29:03.660 --> 00:29:06.420
It all started when we did our Chili's commercial, Angela.
这一切都要从我们拍那支Chili's的广告说起，安吉拉。

653
00:29:06.940 --> 00:29:12.520
And the stylist pulled this, like, gorgeous gold silk blouse for me.
当时造型师给我拿了一件超级好看的金黄色丝绸衬衫。

654
00:29:12.700 --> 00:29:14.220
Yes, you texted me.
对，你给我发过短信。

655
00:29:14.300 --> 00:29:14.640
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

656
00:29:14.760 --> 00:29:17.080
Because we couldn't do our fittings on the same day.
因为我们没法在同一天试装。

657
00:29:17.220 --> 00:29:17.520
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

658
00:29:17.620 --> 00:29:18.600
You went firSt.
你先去的。

659
00:29:18.600 --> 00:29:20.120
And I was like, so what'd they put you in?
我就问，他们让你穿什么？

660
00:29:20.120 --> 00:29:24.200
And you said, I think I'm going to wear this gold-yellow blouse.
你说，我想我会穿那件金黄色的衬衫。

661
00:29:24.280 --> 00:29:26.100
And I was like, are you sure?
我就说，你确定吗？

662
00:29:26.420 --> 00:29:26.840
I know.
我知道。

663
00:29:26.900 --> 00:29:28.680
It sounded a little like, what?
听起来有点，怎么说呢？

664
00:29:28.980 --> 00:29:30.520
It's not a color you normally wear.
那不是你平时会穿的颜色。

665
00:29:30.760 --> 00:29:31.120
No.
没错。

666
00:29:31.360 --> 00:29:34.540
You know, she brought over this rack of clothes,
你知道，她带了一整排衣服过来，

667
00:29:34.560 --> 00:29:35.880
and she was pulling things out,
她一件件拿出来，

668
00:29:35.900 --> 00:29:37.480
and she was like, this is kind of my favorite.
然后说，这件算是我的最爱。

669
00:29:37.480 --> 00:29:38.960
And it was this gold blouse.
就是那件金色的衬衫。

670
00:29:39.000 --> 00:29:40.220
And I said, I don't wear yellow.
我说，我不穿黄色。

671
00:29:40.320 --> 00:29:41.880
I don't think it's going to look good on me.
我觉得我穿起来肯定不好看。

672
00:29:41.920 --> 00:29:41.980
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

673
00:29:42.740 --> 00:29:45.740
And as any good stylist would, she said, give it a try.
作为一个优秀的造型师，她让我试一试。

674
00:29:46.980 --> 00:29:47.920
I loved it.
我爱死它了。

675
00:29:48.020 --> 00:29:48.860
You looked fantastic.
你当时看起来棒极了。

676
00:29:48.960 --> 00:29:50.020
I felt so in love with it.
我太喜欢它了。

677
00:29:50.120 --> 00:29:52.500
That I begged the Chili's people to keep it,
以至于我求Chili's那边的人把它留给我，

678
00:29:52.580 --> 00:29:53.220
and they said yes.
他们答应了。

679
00:29:53.220 --> 00:29:54.320
So I still have it.
所以我现在还留着它。

680
00:29:54.580 --> 00:29:58.040
And then later, you know, I ended up buying a gold sundress.
后来，你知道，我又买了一条金黄色的夏日连衣裙。

681
00:29:58.260 --> 00:30:00.180
I become obsessed with this color yellow,
我变得对这种黄色着了迷，

682
00:30:00.180 --> 00:30:01.740
and Kelly is wearing it.
凯莉也穿了这个颜色。

683
00:30:02.180 --> 00:30:03.200
I don't know.
我不知道。

684
00:30:03.200 --> 00:30:04.020
I'm obsessed.
我太着迷了。

685
00:30:04.180 --> 00:30:06.400
I want to, like, decorate a room in this color.
我想用这种颜色来装饰房间。

686
00:30:06.640 --> 00:30:09.040
But speaking of wardrobe from this episode,
不过说到这一集的服装，

687
00:30:09.280 --> 00:30:11.720
we got a fan question from Lex in Pennsylvania,
我们收到了一位来自宾夕法尼亚州Lex的粉丝提问，

688
00:30:12.420 --> 00:30:16.300
who would like to point out something about Jim's casual wear.
他想指出关于吉姆休闲装的一些细节。

689
00:30:16.840 --> 00:30:17.080
Okay.
好的。

690
00:30:17.080 --> 00:30:19.260
Lex said throughout the series,
Lex说在整部剧里，

691
00:30:19.500 --> 00:30:24.440
Jim wears the same gray sweater and jeans anytime he's out of the office.
吉姆只要不在办公室，穿的都是同一件灰色毛衣和牛仔裤。

692
00:30:24.980 --> 00:30:25.240
Really?
真的吗？

693
00:30:25.480 --> 00:30:30.000
Lex did a mini deep dive and noticed that the gray sweater and jeans combo
Lex做了一次小型深度挖掘，发现这套灰色毛衣加牛仔裤的搭配

694
00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:36.300
shows up in Casual Friday, Andy's Play, Viewing Party, Pool Party, After Hours, and Finale.
出现在了《休闲星期五》、《安迪的戏剧》、《观看派对》、《泳池派对》、《下班后》和《大结局》中。

695
00:30:36.620 --> 00:30:39.160
Lex said, what's the deal with the gray sweater?
Lex问，那件灰色毛衣到底是怎么回事？

696
00:30:40.420 --> 00:30:42.060
I think that's kind of cute.
我觉得这挺可爱的。

697
00:30:42.060 --> 00:30:45.300
I kind of feel like he has his favorite kind of hangout sweater.
我觉得他可能就是有自己最喜欢的休闲毛衣。

698
00:30:45.600 --> 00:30:45.860
Yeah.
是啊。

699
00:30:46.280 --> 00:30:47.840
I kind of love it, too.
我也挺喜欢的。

700
00:30:47.960 --> 00:30:49.700
And you're right, Lex.
你说得对，Lex。

701
00:30:49.800 --> 00:30:53.860
Like, once you pointed it out, I realized, yeah, he does every time.
就像你指出来的那样，我意识到，没错，他每次都这样。

702
00:30:54.300 --> 00:30:55.640
Wears the same sweater.
穿同一件毛衣。

703
00:30:56.260 --> 00:30:59.380
So Andy's going to explain that they're staying late tonight
所以安迪要解释说他们今晚要留下来加班

704
00:30:59.380 --> 00:31:02.800
to service the accounts of the employees who are in Florida.
去处理那些在佛罗里达的员工的账户。

705
00:31:03.120 --> 00:31:03.540
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

706
00:31:04.120 --> 00:31:07.040
Pam does point out they could have been doing that all along, but whatever.
帕姆确实指出了他们本来一直都可以这么做，但无所谓了。

707
00:31:07.500 --> 00:31:08.880
They're now going to stay late.
他们现在要留下来加班了。

708
00:31:09.280 --> 00:31:12.100
I loved how Pam popped into Andy's talking head.
我喜欢帕姆突然出现在安迪采访镜头里的那一幕。

709
00:31:12.320 --> 00:31:13.020
Yeah, that was cute.
是啊，那很可爱。

710
00:31:13.020 --> 00:31:15.120
I remember when we shot that, I was so excited
我记得拍那场戏的时候，我特别兴奋

711
00:31:15.120 --> 00:31:18.180
because you always see Dwight doing that to Michael.
因为你总是看到德怀特对迈克尔做那种事。

712
00:31:18.380 --> 00:31:18.560
Yeah.
没错。

713
00:31:18.560 --> 00:31:21.460
And I was so delighted to get to do it.
能轮到我做，我真是太高兴了。

714
00:31:21.640 --> 00:31:22.320
I know.
我知道。

715
00:31:22.420 --> 00:31:22.700
I know.
我知道。

716
00:31:22.780 --> 00:31:26.500
It's a classic office moment where you're in the boss's office,
这是办公室里的经典时刻，你待在老板办公室里，

717
00:31:26.500 --> 00:31:29.820
you think the boss is alone, and then someone pops in.
以为老板是一个人，结果有人突然冒出来。

718
00:31:29.960 --> 00:31:32.000
We all coveted this bit.
我们所有人都很想演这个桥段。

719
00:31:32.160 --> 00:31:36.480
I got to do it one time with Michael when I'm hemming his pants.
我有一次和迈克尔演过，当时我在帮他缝裤边。

720
00:31:36.500 --> 00:31:37.100
I remember.
我记得。

721
00:31:37.580 --> 00:31:38.640
I love it.
我喜欢那个。

722
00:31:39.160 --> 00:31:42.200
Well, Halstead said this idea of the office staying late at work,
嗯，霍尔斯特德说办公室加班这个点子，

723
00:31:42.200 --> 00:31:47.040
that storyline needed to happen because they needed to have a nighttime storyline
这个故事情节必须得有，因为他们需要一个夜间剧情

724
00:31:47.040 --> 00:31:51.180
for the people at the office to mirror what was happening in Tallahassee.
来让办公室里的人和塔拉哈西发生的事情相呼应。

725
00:31:51.360 --> 00:31:53.260
For purposes of the documentary, right?
为了纪录片的拍摄效果，对吧？

726
00:31:53.260 --> 00:31:54.120
Yes, exactly.
没错，正是这样。

727
00:31:54.400 --> 00:31:58.200
But Halstead said it was very easy for them to come up with funny bits
但霍尔斯特德说，他们想出这些搞笑桥段非常容易，

728
00:31:58.200 --> 00:32:04.640
for this office storyline because the writers often stayed at work until about 10 o'clock
因为编剧们经常在办公室待到晚上10点左右

729
00:32:04.640 --> 00:32:10.280
working on scripts, and they would get punchy, or people would shout things out,
忙着写剧本，他们会变得很亢奋，或者有人会大喊大叫，

730
00:32:10.540 --> 00:32:12.880
or food would come.
或者会有食物送来。

731
00:32:12.880 --> 00:32:16.400
Anyway, they drew on their personal experience for this storyline.
总之，他们从自己的亲身经历中汲取了灵感来创作这个故事。

732
00:32:17.100 --> 00:32:22.280
Well, you know, I was really curious about the idea of working after closing time
嗯，你知道，我真的很好奇下班后工作这个概念，

733
00:32:22.280 --> 00:32:25.020
and where the term after hours came from.
以及下班后（after hours）这个词是怎么来的。

734
00:32:25.260 --> 00:32:26.880
So here's what I found.
所以我查了一下。

735
00:32:26.880 --> 00:32:30.380
It's an expression that became popular in the 1800s.
这是一个在19世纪流行起来的表达。

736
00:32:31.260 --> 00:32:31.940
1800s?
19世纪？

737
00:32:31.940 --> 00:32:32.280
Yes.
是的。

738
00:32:32.540 --> 00:32:34.100
The phrase after hours?
下班后这个短语？

739
00:32:34.380 --> 00:32:34.720
Yes.
是的。

740
00:32:35.220 --> 00:32:40.020
It originated when governments passed certain laws to regulate business hours.
它起源于政府通过某些法律来规范营业时间的时候。

741
00:32:40.260 --> 00:32:40.620
Oh.
哦。

742
00:32:40.740 --> 00:32:44.920
And once businesses were meant to close, it became after hours.
一旦企业被要求关门，那之后的时间就成了下班后。

743
00:32:44.920 --> 00:32:50.980
So it also gave rise to the term after hours club for a drinking club that remained open
所以它也引出了下班后俱乐部这个词，指那些营业时间

744
00:32:50.980 --> 00:32:53.640
later than legal establishments.
比合法场所更晚的酒吧。

745
00:32:54.620 --> 00:32:54.860
Oh.
哦。

746
00:32:55.280 --> 00:32:55.680
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

747
00:32:56.280 --> 00:32:56.440
Yeah.
是啊。

748
00:32:56.660 --> 00:32:59.640
So the term after hours has been around for a long time.
所以下班后这个词已经存在很长时间了。

749
00:33:00.180 --> 00:33:00.480
Wow.
哇。

750
00:33:00.860 --> 00:33:01.200
I don't know.
我不知道。

751
00:33:01.420 --> 00:33:06.380
Well, speaking of after hours drinking, everyone in Tallahassee is at the bar.
说到下班后的聚会，塔拉哈西的所有人都在酒吧里。

752
00:33:06.660 --> 00:33:07.040
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

753
00:33:07.040 --> 00:33:13.940
Packer and Nellie disagree on who would win in a fight between Jason Bourne and James Bond.
帕克和内莉在争论杰森·伯恩和詹姆斯·邦德打架谁会赢。

754
00:33:14.480 --> 00:33:18.060
Who do you think would win in a fight between Jason Bourne and James Bond?
你觉得杰森·伯恩和詹姆斯·邦德打架谁会赢？

755
00:33:18.200 --> 00:33:22.340
Because I checked all the message boards and there is a very clear opinion on the matter.
因为我查了所有的留言板，大家对此有非常明确的看法。

756
00:33:22.900 --> 00:33:24.360
100% Jason Bourne.
百分之百是杰森·伯恩。

757
00:33:24.560 --> 00:33:25.420
You're correct.
你说得对。

758
00:33:26.020 --> 00:33:26.520
Yeah.
是啊。

759
00:33:26.840 --> 00:33:30.480
I mean, he knows how many paces from where he's sitting to the door.
我是说，他知道从他坐的地方到门口有多少步。

760
00:33:30.480 --> 00:33:36.600
He just has a lot more experience with hand-to-hand combat, is what everyone said.
大家都说，他在肉搏战方面的经验要丰富得多。

761
00:33:36.780 --> 00:33:40.320
I got curious who would win a fight between Jason Bourne and John Wick.
我很好奇杰森·伯恩和约翰·威克打架谁会赢。

762
00:33:40.800 --> 00:33:41.880
Oh, gosh.
天哪。

763
00:33:42.620 --> 00:33:44.140
Why you got to do that to me?
你为什么要这么为难我？

764
00:33:44.420 --> 00:33:45.620
Why do I have to pick?
为什么非要我选？

765
00:33:45.780 --> 00:33:48.220
Well, the fan forums say Jason Bourne again.
粉丝论坛上说还是杰森·伯恩会赢。

766
00:33:48.840 --> 00:33:51.420
Apparently, Jason Bourne is just the sh**.
显然，杰森·伯恩就是牛逼。

767
00:33:51.420 --> 00:33:52.060
Yeah.
是啊。

768
00:33:52.840 --> 00:34:00.560
Have you seen John Wick, like, drive a car with one arm and shoot out the other side doing a 360?
你见过约翰·威克单手开车，另一只手伸出窗外做360度旋转射击吗？

769
00:34:00.980 --> 00:34:01.540
Come on.
拜托。

770
00:34:01.540 --> 00:34:04.460
Listen, if you give John Wick a car, I think—
听着，如果你给约翰·威克一辆车，我觉得——

771
00:34:04.460 --> 00:34:07.900
And a ton of, like, nunchucks and ammo.
还有一大堆双节棍和弹药。

772
00:34:08.120 --> 00:34:09.660
Or a giant sword.
或者一把大剑。

773
00:34:10.460 --> 00:34:10.940
He's—
他——

774
00:34:10.940 --> 00:34:11.300
Oh, man.
天呐。

775
00:34:11.300 --> 00:34:11.760
I don't know.
我不知道。

776
00:34:11.880 --> 00:34:12.880
I'm going John Wick.
我选约翰·威克。

777
00:34:13.140 --> 00:34:19.920
Well, I mean, fan forums just really think that Jason Bourne, I guess, is the beSt.
我是说，粉丝论坛真的觉得杰森·伯恩才是最强的。

778
00:34:19.920 --> 00:34:23.900
Listen, if you let Jason Bourne get up close to you, you're done-zo.
听着，如果你让杰森·伯恩近身，你就完蛋了。

779
00:34:24.180 --> 00:34:24.780
You're done-zo.
你就彻底完蛋了。

780
00:34:24.940 --> 00:34:25.100
Yeah.
是啊。

781
00:34:25.540 --> 00:34:27.620
But maybe John Wick could get him from a distance.
但也许约翰·威克能从远处干掉他。

782
00:34:28.000 --> 00:34:32.140
Well, Dwight's money is on Genghis Khan because he was willing to kill children.
德怀特押的是成吉思汗，因为他连孩子都杀。

783
00:34:32.360 --> 00:34:33.140
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

784
00:34:33.240 --> 00:34:34.840
Dwight always makes it weird.
德怀特总是把气氛搞得很怪。

785
00:34:35.160 --> 00:34:36.980
He always makes it so awkward.
他总是让场面变得那么尴尬。

786
00:34:37.420 --> 00:34:45.260
There are so many more moments like this that were in the shooting draft and in deleted scenes where Dwight takes it one step too weird.
剧本初稿和删减片段里还有很多这样的时刻，德怀特总是会把事情搞得过分诡异。

787
00:34:45.280 --> 00:34:46.340
It's so bizarre.
真是太离谱了。

788
00:34:46.340 --> 00:34:54.440
He said, there's a moment, Jenna, where Dwight is trying to flirt with Nellie and he's trying to one-up Packer.
他说，珍娜，有个片段是德怀特试图调戏内莉，还想压过帕克一头。

789
00:34:55.340 --> 00:34:57.860
Nellie says to Packer, ooh, innuendo.
内莉对帕克说，噢，话里有话啊（innuendo）。

790
00:34:58.160 --> 00:35:01.020
And Dwight jumps in and goes, in your endo?
结果德怀特插嘴说，在你后面（in your endo）？

791
00:35:01.240 --> 00:35:01.640
No!
不！

792
00:35:02.160 --> 00:35:04.380
And Nellie goes, watch it.
然后内莉说，注意点。

793
00:35:04.540 --> 00:35:05.320
Watch it.
注意点。

794
00:35:05.420 --> 00:35:06.560
Like, all right.
就像是，好吧。

795
00:35:07.360 --> 00:35:08.760
Just pump the brakes.
收敛一点吧。

796
00:35:09.020 --> 00:35:11.700
There were so many more moments like this is all I'm saying.
我只是想说，还有很多这样的时刻。

797
00:35:11.700 --> 00:35:19.320
Oh, well, meanwhile, Ryan and Erin are sitting together and Ryan orders a Chardonnay and Erin orders a waffle.
噢，与此同时，瑞安和艾琳坐在一起，瑞安点了一杯霞多丽，艾琳点了一个华夫饼。

798
00:35:19.560 --> 00:35:20.000
No, no, no.
不，不，不。

799
00:35:20.140 --> 00:35:20.360
What?
什么？

800
00:35:20.360 --> 00:35:23.680
He orders the oakiest Chardonnay they have.
他点了他们店里橡木味最浓的霞多丽。

801
00:35:23.800 --> 00:35:26.120
What is with the writers and oaky?
编剧们是怎么回事，为什么老提橡木味？

802
00:35:26.600 --> 00:35:28.480
They love oaky afterbirth.
他们就喜欢那种橡木味的余韵。

803
00:35:28.700 --> 00:35:29.120
I know.
我知道。

804
00:35:29.280 --> 00:35:29.640
Oaky.
橡木味。

805
00:35:30.140 --> 00:35:30.800
You know what?
你知道吗？

806
00:35:30.880 --> 00:35:31.900
They don't have any waffles.
他们根本没有华夫饼。

807
00:35:32.280 --> 00:35:35.000
Yeah, and Erin knows what she wants and it's a hotel waffle.
是啊，艾琳知道她想要什么，她想要酒店那种华夫饼。

808
00:35:35.740 --> 00:35:40.980
Well, this is when Erin decides to tell Ryan about her plan to stay in Florida.
嗯，就在这时，艾琳决定告诉瑞安她打算留在佛罗里达。

809
00:35:41.420 --> 00:35:46.680
And I guess Ryan sees this as the perfect opportunity to hook up with her and then not have to deal with her.
我猜瑞安觉得这是个绝佳的机会，可以跟她搞在一起，然后就不用再应付她了。

810
00:35:46.880 --> 00:35:48.220
Yeah, exactly.
没错，就是这样。

811
00:35:48.520 --> 00:35:49.740
So now that's his mission.
所以现在这就是他的任务了。

812
00:35:50.460 --> 00:35:51.840
I'm going to hook up with Erin.
我要去跟艾琳搞在一起。

813
00:35:52.100 --> 00:35:53.380
I'm going to get her a waffle.
我要给她弄个华夫饼。

814
00:35:53.680 --> 00:35:54.520
That's my way in.
这就是我的切入点。

815
00:35:54.760 --> 00:36:00.400
Back in the conference room at Dunder Mifflin, the late night work jam is underway.
回到邓德·米福林的会议室，深夜加班正在进行中。

816
00:36:01.100 --> 00:36:04.000
But Kelly, Kelly cannot take it.
但是凯莉，凯莉受不了了。

817
00:36:04.000 --> 00:36:04.680
She can't take it.
她真的受不了了。

818
00:36:04.680 --> 00:36:06.320
This is how the scene starts.
这一幕就是这样开始的。

819
00:36:06.980 --> 00:36:09.500
Pam says, Watson, carpet and tile.
帕姆说，沃森，地毯和瓷砖。

820
00:36:09.860 --> 00:36:11.320
Kevin says, one order.
凯文说，一份订单。

821
00:36:11.940 --> 00:36:16.880
Oscar says, order reference number 00983-126.
奥斯卡说，订单参考编号00983-126。

822
00:36:17.200 --> 00:36:20.420
Phyllis says, eight cases bright white inkjet.
菲利斯说，八箱亮白喷墨打印纸。

823
00:36:20.800 --> 00:36:22.020
Angela says, paid.
安吉拉说，已付款。

824
00:36:22.420 --> 00:36:24.120
Kelly yells, I'm dying.
凯莉大喊，我要死了。

825
00:36:25.200 --> 00:36:26.660
Daryl says, processed.
达里尔说，已处理。

826
00:36:26.860 --> 00:36:28.060
Val says, and delivered.
瓦尔说，已送达。

827
00:36:28.740 --> 00:36:34.220
So Halston and Warren reminded me about the very real life inspiration for Kelly's line.
所以哈尔斯顿和沃伦提醒了我，凯莉那句台词在现实生活中是有真实原型的。

828
00:36:34.220 --> 00:36:36.620
And as soon as they reminded me, I started laughing.
他们一提醒我，我就笑了起来。

829
00:36:37.540 --> 00:36:38.940
Oh, my God, lady.
天哪，女士。

830
00:36:39.160 --> 00:36:40.300
I remembered it instantly.
我立刻就想起来了。

831
00:36:40.300 --> 00:36:42.860
It was like a wave of memories had washed over me.
就像一阵回忆的浪潮向我涌来。

832
00:36:42.980 --> 00:36:44.320
You have to share this story.
你一定要分享一下这个故事。

833
00:36:45.020 --> 00:36:48.440
So you guys know that I love to host a Yankee Swap party.
你们都知道我喜欢举办“洋基交换”派对吧。

834
00:36:48.440 --> 00:36:51.000
You know, I was inspired by our show.
你知道，我是受我们剧的启发。

835
00:36:51.180 --> 00:36:52.380
I started hosting one.
我开始举办这种派对。

836
00:36:52.620 --> 00:36:59.440
Well, one year, one year, a friend of ours brought a new date.
有那么一年，我们的一位朋友带了一位新约会对象来。

837
00:36:59.520 --> 00:37:01.660
We're all like, ooh, who's the new gal?
我们都觉得，噢，这位新来的姑娘是谁呀？

838
00:37:02.120 --> 00:37:04.060
We were playing Yankee Swap.
我们当时正在玩“洋基交换”。

839
00:37:04.140 --> 00:37:05.660
And I guess she didn't care for it.
我猜她并不喜欢这个游戏。

840
00:37:05.800 --> 00:37:09.840
And just out of the blue, she literally said, I'm dying.
然后她突然没头没脑地说了句，我要死了。

841
00:37:10.540 --> 00:37:12.180
Like, she hated the game.
就好像她讨厌这个游戏一样。

842
00:37:12.440 --> 00:37:13.800
She was so miserable.
她当时太痛苦了。

843
00:37:13.800 --> 00:37:15.580
I think she was really bored by us.
我觉得她真的觉得我们很无聊。

844
00:37:15.660 --> 00:37:20.480
She also said at one time, well, I'm pretty sure none of you have traveled as much as I have.
她当时还说，嗯，我很确定你们谁都没我旅游去过的地方多。

845
00:37:20.900 --> 00:37:23.900
She was like pissing people off left and right.
她简直是在到处惹人生气。

846
00:37:24.480 --> 00:37:30.000
But Halston said, when she said, I'm dying, to him, it felt like more like a verbal slip,
但哈尔斯顿说，当她说“我要死了”的时候，对他来说，这更像是一种口误，

847
00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:32.500
like from her real true life inner monologue.
就像是她内心真实想法的流露。

848
00:37:32.640 --> 00:37:32.980
Yes.
没错。

849
00:37:33.200 --> 00:37:35.200
And he and Warren thought it was hilarious.
他和沃伦觉得这太搞笑了。

850
00:37:35.200 --> 00:37:37.840
They remembered it, and they wrote it into this episode.
他们记住了这一点，并把它写进了这一集里。

851
00:37:37.840 --> 00:37:42.820
This is my favorite thing about writers, is how they just file away little moments.
我最喜欢作家的一点，就是他们如何把生活中的小瞬间归档保存。

852
00:37:42.960 --> 00:37:44.520
They observe, and they file away.
他们观察，然后归档。

853
00:37:44.520 --> 00:37:47.120
They're like, that'll come out of the file at just the right time.
他们会想，这些素材总会在最合适的时机派上用场。

854
00:37:47.120 --> 00:37:48.560
And this was it with Kelly.
凯莉的情况就是这样。

855
00:37:48.800 --> 00:37:49.340
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

856
00:37:49.420 --> 00:37:50.720
Warren and I were talking yesterday.
沃伦和我昨天还在聊这个。

857
00:37:50.720 --> 00:37:52.820
We were cracking up about this moment.
我们聊到这个瞬间时笑得不行。

858
00:37:53.280 --> 00:38:00.140
Ah, this whole Nellie, Packer, Dwight, flirty triangle is now going on strong.
啊，内莉、帕克和德怀特之间这种调情三角关系现在正愈演愈烈。

859
00:38:00.460 --> 00:38:00.960
Oh, gosh.
噢，天哪。

860
00:38:00.960 --> 00:38:01.900
It's so uncomfortable.
真是太尴尬了。

861
00:38:02.480 --> 00:38:05.580
Packer's like, hey, the cowgirl has chosen her saddle.
帕克说，嘿，牛仔女郎已经选好了她的马鞍。

862
00:38:07.440 --> 00:38:08.160
Like that?
喜欢那样吗？

863
00:38:08.400 --> 00:38:08.520
Yeah.
是的。

864
00:38:08.660 --> 00:38:10.900
That was not in the script.
那句台词剧本里没有。

865
00:38:10.980 --> 00:38:11.500
It wasn't.
确实没有。

866
00:38:11.740 --> 00:38:13.240
That was just Dave Koechner.
那是戴夫·科恩纳的即兴发挥。

867
00:38:13.240 --> 00:38:14.220
That's a Koechner special.
那是科恩纳的招牌动作。

868
00:38:14.420 --> 00:38:20.760
But then Rain matched it as Dwight, which is so funny, because he did it as only Dwight
但雷恩作为德怀特接住了这个梗，这太搞笑了，因为他演出了德怀特独有的那种感觉，

869
00:38:20.760 --> 00:38:22.480
would do it, like kind of cringey.
就是那种让人尴尬的感觉。

870
00:38:22.660 --> 00:38:23.760
I mean, they're both cringey.
我是说，他们俩都让人尴尬。

871
00:38:24.420 --> 00:38:25.800
Dwight says, you know what?
德怀特说，你知道吗？

872
00:38:25.800 --> 00:38:29.200
If anyone's going to sleep with Nellie for personal gain, it's going to be him.
如果有人要为了个人利益跟内莉上床，那个人只能是他。

873
00:38:29.640 --> 00:38:33.460
Well, there was a candy bag alt for this Dwight talking head.
其实这段德怀特的采访镜头还有一个糖果袋的备选方案。

874
00:38:33.460 --> 00:38:34.440
Please tell me.
快告诉我。

875
00:38:34.660 --> 00:38:36.160
It was a must shoot.
那是必拍镜头。

876
00:38:36.420 --> 00:38:36.660
Okay.
好吧。

877
00:38:37.120 --> 00:38:38.900
So you know it lives out there somewhere.
所以你知道它肯定流落在某个地方。

878
00:38:39.260 --> 00:38:45.060
Dwight would have said, if I can get ahead by shaking a certain hand, patting a back
德怀特本来说的是，如果我能通过握某人的手、拍拍背，

879
00:38:45.060 --> 00:38:49.960
or, you know, and then he motions to his penis, I'll do it.
或者，你知道的，然后他指了指自己的下体，我就能获得晋升，那我就干。

880
00:38:50.540 --> 00:38:51.940
This is a team effort.
这是团队协作。

881
00:38:52.200 --> 00:38:54.680
No part of Dwight Schrute sits on the bench.
德怀特·舒特身上没有任何一部分会坐冷板凳。

882
00:38:55.160 --> 00:38:56.020
Oh, wow.
噢，哇。

883
00:38:56.580 --> 00:38:57.100
Okay.
好吧。

884
00:38:57.260 --> 00:38:59.500
All hands on deck, if you will.
可以说是全员出动了。

885
00:39:01.440 --> 00:39:06.760
Well, meanwhile, back in the conference room, Andy has brought in dinner.
与此同时，在会议室里，安迪带了晚餐过来。

886
00:39:06.960 --> 00:39:08.020
A nice gesture.
真是个好意。

887
00:39:08.320 --> 00:39:08.560
Yeah.
是啊。

888
00:39:08.760 --> 00:39:12.980
And he wants everyone to know it's not pizza or tacos.
而且他想让大家知道，这不是披萨也不是塔可饼。

889
00:39:13.460 --> 00:39:15.240
He went another way with it.
他换了个路子。

890
00:39:15.340 --> 00:39:19.580
It's a Jamaican feast brought to them by Val's boyfriend, Brandon.
这是一顿牙买加盛宴，是瓦尔的男朋友布兰登送来的。

891
00:39:19.960 --> 00:39:21.000
Yeah, her boyf.
对，她男票。

892
00:39:21.080 --> 00:39:21.520
Her boyf.
她男票。

893
00:39:22.160 --> 00:39:22.400
Yeah.
是啊。

894
00:39:22.580 --> 00:39:23.700
Bringing in the food.
送吃的来了。

895
00:39:24.520 --> 00:39:25.480
Phyllis is snarky.
菲利斯说话带刺。

896
00:39:25.640 --> 00:39:29.220
She says, if I want a Jamaican food, I'd just hire a bodyguard and go there.
她说，如果我想吃牙买加菜，我直接雇个保镖去那儿吃就行了。

897
00:39:29.760 --> 00:39:31.640
Oscar tries to bond with Brandon.
奥斯卡试图和布兰登套近乎。

898
00:39:31.880 --> 00:39:35.000
He says, oh, man, I was just reading about these elections in Jamaica.
他说，天哪，我刚好在读关于牙买加选举的新闻。

899
00:39:35.180 --> 00:39:37.240
And Brandon's like, yeah, yeah, no, I'm not from Jamaica.
结果布兰登说，是啊是啊，不，我不是牙买加人。

900
00:39:37.820 --> 00:39:38.000
Yeah.
是啊。

901
00:39:38.380 --> 00:39:43.800
I noticed, Angela, right after Phyllis says that line, you itch your nose real big.
安吉拉，我注意到在菲利斯说完那句台词后，你用力挠了挠鼻子。

902
00:39:44.940 --> 00:39:46.720
Like super big nose itch.
就是那种特别用力的鼻子瘙痒。

903
00:39:47.000 --> 00:39:47.380
Okay.
好吧。

904
00:39:47.760 --> 00:39:48.340
I don't know.
我不知道。

905
00:39:49.940 --> 00:39:51.760
Sometimes those are the things you see.
有时候你就会注意到这些细节。

906
00:39:51.940 --> 00:39:53.500
Maybe someone was thinking of me.
也许当时有人在想我。

907
00:39:53.900 --> 00:39:54.260
Oh, yeah.
哦，是啊。

908
00:39:54.440 --> 00:39:56.800
Doesn't your nose get itchy if someone's thinking of you?
如果有人在想你，你的鼻子不会发痒吗？

909
00:39:56.800 --> 00:39:57.860
Is that a thing?
有这种说法吗？

910
00:39:58.000 --> 00:39:59.060
That's what my mom always says.
我妈总是这么说。

911
00:39:59.060 --> 00:39:59.620
I remember.
我记得。

912
00:39:59.700 --> 00:40:00.860
Yes, I remember that.
是的，我记得那个。

913
00:40:01.300 --> 00:40:01.680
Aw.
噢。

914
00:40:02.080 --> 00:40:03.700
Well, someone was thinking of you in that moment.
好吧，那一刻确实有人在想你。

915
00:40:03.940 --> 00:40:04.760
You'll always have it.
你会一直记得的。

916
00:40:04.920 --> 00:40:06.880
Or I just had a runny nose or something.
或者我当时只是流鼻涕什么的。

917
00:40:07.080 --> 00:40:07.460
I don't know.
我不知道。

918
00:40:07.480 --> 00:40:07.820
One of the two.
二者必居其一。

919
00:40:08.680 --> 00:40:11.520
Daryl is going to introduce himself to Brandon.
达里尔准备向布兰登做自我介绍。

920
00:40:11.780 --> 00:40:12.100
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

921
00:40:12.360 --> 00:40:16.280
And then Brandon immediately accuses him of sleeping with Val.
然后布兰登立刻指责他跟瓦尔睡过。

922
00:40:16.760 --> 00:40:18.600
Oh, F-bombs were dropped.
哦，当时可是脏话连篇。

923
00:40:18.760 --> 00:40:19.060
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

924
00:40:19.560 --> 00:40:22.300
I love everything about Jerry Miner in this episode.
这一集里杰里·迈纳的一切我都喜欢。

925
00:40:22.300 --> 00:40:25.380
But one of my favorite lines of his is in this scene.
但他最让我喜欢的台词之一就在这一幕里。

926
00:40:25.640 --> 00:40:28.380
It's when Brandon says, I hope you all like goat.
就是布兰登说“希望你们都喜欢羊肉”的时候。

927
00:40:28.680 --> 00:40:29.080
Yeah.
是啊。

928
00:40:29.560 --> 00:40:31.280
I wasn't even sure if that was scripted.
我甚至不确定那是不是剧本写的。

929
00:40:31.360 --> 00:40:31.960
I went to the script.
我查了剧本。

930
00:40:32.100 --> 00:40:33.000
It is scripted.
那是剧本写的。

931
00:40:33.420 --> 00:40:35.800
Warren was like, it was scripted.
沃伦说，那是剧本写的。

932
00:40:35.880 --> 00:40:38.260
But I have to give all credit to Jerry Miner.
但我必须把所有功劳都归给杰里·迈纳。

933
00:40:38.380 --> 00:40:40.160
The way he delivered it steals the show.
他演绎的方式简直抢尽了风头。

934
00:40:40.160 --> 00:40:42.580
I thought the not baby girl was improvised.
我原以为“不是小宝贝”那句是即兴发挥的。

935
00:40:42.860 --> 00:40:44.300
When Angela says, is it spicy?
当安吉拉问“这很辣吗？”的时候。

936
00:40:44.300 --> 00:40:46.260
He just throws that away so perfectly.
