00:47:34.380 --> 00:47:37.440
And, you know, they said texting etiquette at this time.
而且，你知道，他们当时谈论的是短信礼仪。

1098
00:47:37.440 --> 00:47:39.320
We were talking about it a lot.
我们当时讨论了很多。

1099
00:47:39.600 --> 00:47:40.980
It was still new, guys.
那时候这还是新鲜事物，伙计们。

1100
00:47:40.980 --> 00:47:41.680
We're old.
我们老了。

1101
00:47:41.780 --> 00:47:43.020
This is old tech stuff.
这是老旧的技术玩意儿。

1102
00:47:43.080 --> 00:47:43.980
It kind of is.
确实有点。

1103
00:47:44.280 --> 00:47:49.380
But they really like the idea that texting late at night is something that would get Daryl into trouble.
但他们真的很喜欢这个点子，就是深夜发短信会让达里尔惹上麻烦。

1104
00:47:49.380 --> 00:47:49.780
Yeah.
是啊。

1105
00:47:51.180 --> 00:47:52.880
This scene would have continued.
这场戏本来还会继续的。

1106
00:47:53.420 --> 00:47:54.420
It was longer.
原本更长一些。

1107
00:47:54.660 --> 00:48:00.180
And in the end, Brandon goes storming out with Val chasing after him.
最后，布兰登气冲冲地跑了出去，瓦尔在后面追他。

1108
00:48:00.440 --> 00:48:02.460
Here's what it said in the shooting draft.
剧本初稿里是这么写的。

1109
00:48:02.640 --> 00:48:02.840
Okay.
好的。

1110
00:48:03.580 --> 00:48:06.080
Val chases after him, leaving Daryl upset.
瓦尔追了出去，留下达里尔心烦意乱。

1111
00:48:06.660 --> 00:48:08.100
Everyone silent.
大家沉默不语。

1112
00:48:08.960 --> 00:48:12.080
Andy produces a pump and some balloons from his pocket.
安迪从口袋里掏出一个打气筒和一些气球。

1113
00:48:12.860 --> 00:48:14.360
Andy says to Meredith,
安迪对梅雷迪思说：

1114
00:48:14.900 --> 00:48:20.120
Meredith, if you could have any balloon animal in the world that was either a dog or a snake, which would it be?
梅雷迪思，如果全世界的气球动物任你选，只能选狗或蛇，你会选哪一个？

1115
00:48:21.340 --> 00:48:22.380
Wait, lady.
等等，女士。

1116
00:48:22.640 --> 00:48:29.840
I feel like memories are flooding back to me of shooting this with Ed, like, pumping the balloon.
我感觉和艾德拍这一幕的记忆都涌上来了，比如，给气球打气。

1117
00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:31.280
Trying to make these balloons.
试着做这些气球。

1118
00:48:31.700 --> 00:48:33.500
And they were all horrible.
它们全都丑得要命。

1119
00:48:33.800 --> 00:48:34.240
They were terrible.
太糟糕了。

1120
00:48:34.340 --> 00:48:35.140
They were terrible.
简直惨不忍睹。

1121
00:48:35.420 --> 00:48:42.540
So, you guys, if you notice a bunch of weird-looking balloon animals on the conference room table,
所以，各位，如果你们注意到会议桌上有一堆奇形怪状的气球动物，

1122
00:48:42.540 --> 00:48:44.580
they were Ed Helms' attempts.
那都是艾德·赫尔姆斯的作品。

1123
00:48:45.620 --> 00:48:47.440
I am so remembering this now.
我现在完全想起来了。

1124
00:48:47.580 --> 00:48:48.560
We laughed so hard.
我们当时笑得好厉害。

1125
00:48:48.740 --> 00:48:54.080
Because I think, you know, the people who do balloon animals, they make it look so easy.
因为我觉得，你知道，那些会做气球动物的人，他们让这看起来太简单了。

1126
00:48:54.400 --> 00:48:54.500
I know.
我懂。

1127
00:48:54.680 --> 00:48:56.980
And I think we just all took for granted.
我觉得我们当时都想当然了。

1128
00:48:56.980 --> 00:49:03.560
Like, the writers, Brian as director, Ed, all of us that just, like, he could just make something.
编剧们、导演布莱恩、艾德，我们所有人都觉得，他随手就能做出点什么来。

1129
00:49:03.700 --> 00:49:06.780
And we knew, like, oh, they're not going to come out great.
我们当时就知道，哦，它们肯定做不好。

1130
00:49:06.780 --> 00:49:12.040
But, like, this was, like, he couldn't even get them to, like, he couldn't even make an X.
但是，他甚至连个X形状都做不出来。

1131
00:49:12.200 --> 00:49:14.940
Like, he could do—they just kept flying everywhere.
他只能——气球一直到处乱飞。

1132
00:49:15.040 --> 00:49:15.180
Yeah.
是啊。

1133
00:49:15.400 --> 00:49:16.240
And also—
而且——

1134
00:49:16.240 --> 00:49:16.780
So hard.
太难了。

1135
00:49:16.900 --> 00:49:19.860
Also, it was way more pumping than I think—
而且，打气的时间比我想象的要多得多——

1136
00:49:19.860 --> 00:49:21.400
There was so much pumping time.
打气的时间太长了。

1137
00:49:21.820 --> 00:49:24.200
There was so much time spent pumping the balloons.
花在给气球打气上的时间太多了。

1138
00:49:24.380 --> 00:49:25.120
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1139
00:49:25.380 --> 00:49:27.140
What a fun thing to remember.
真是段有趣的回忆。

1140
00:49:27.320 --> 00:49:28.060
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1141
00:49:28.060 --> 00:49:29.800
I was cracking up.
我当时笑得不行。

1142
00:49:29.880 --> 00:49:32.280
And, you know, part of it's in deleted scenes.
而且，你知道，其中一部分在删减片段里。

1143
00:49:32.280 --> 00:49:35.820
But then you see the balloons on the conference table in later scenes.
但在后来的戏份里，你还能看到会议桌上的那些气球。

1144
00:49:36.000 --> 00:49:36.860
They're so awful.
它们太丑了。

1145
00:49:36.960 --> 00:49:37.560
They're awful.
简直没法看。

1146
00:49:37.740 --> 00:49:40.540
And this was Andy's way of, like, easing the tension.
这是安迪想要缓解紧张气氛的方式。

1147
00:49:42.000 --> 00:49:43.060
Oh, my goodness.
我的天呐。

1148
00:49:43.420 --> 00:49:45.620
Oh, thank you for reminding me of that.
谢谢你提醒我这件事。

1149
00:49:45.980 --> 00:49:50.960
Well, things might have taken a turn for Tallahassee back in Tallahassee.
好吧，回到塔拉哈西，事情可能已经发生了转折。

1150
00:49:51.000 --> 00:49:54.400
Because now, Packer is doing the cherry stem thing.
因为现在，帕克正在玩那个樱桃梗的把戏。

1151
00:49:54.580 --> 00:49:54.920
Yes.
是的。

1152
00:49:54.920 --> 00:49:56.900
Or he's tying it with his tongue into a knot.
或者他正用舌头把樱桃梗打成结。

1153
00:49:56.900 --> 00:50:03.780
And this made me laugh so hard when Dwight says, please, anyone can tie a knot.
德怀特说“拜托，谁都能打个结”的时候，我真的笑得不行。

1154
00:50:03.940 --> 00:50:05.880
The real talent's in untying it.
真正的本事是解开它。

1155
00:50:06.020 --> 00:50:12.240
And he takes the cherry stem that was in Packer's mouth and puts it in his mouth.
然后他把帕克嘴里的那根樱桃梗拿出来，放进了自己嘴里。

1156
00:50:12.500 --> 00:50:15.880
And then he works real hard to untie it.
接着他非常努力地去解开它。

1157
00:50:16.100 --> 00:50:20.200
You guys, in deleted scenes, this moment plays out.
伙计们，在删减片段里，有这一幕。

1158
00:50:20.500 --> 00:50:23.600
And Rain as Dwight is really struggling.
雷恩饰演的德怀特当时真的很费劲。

1159
00:50:23.600 --> 00:50:27.260
Like, he's working so hard on that cherry stem.
他为了那根樱桃梗真的拼尽全力。

1160
00:50:27.440 --> 00:50:32.560
And there is just this awkward silence as Nellie and Packer watch Dwight.
奈莉和帕克看着德怀特，现场陷入了一阵尴尬的沉默。

1161
00:50:32.880 --> 00:50:36.540
And then ultimately, he unknotts it.
最终，他把结解开了。

1162
00:50:36.620 --> 00:50:38.260
And he spits it out.
然后他把它吐了出来。

1163
00:50:38.480 --> 00:50:39.840
And then he holds it up.
接着他把它举了起来。

1164
00:50:39.900 --> 00:50:43.180
And he goes, there it is, straight enough to pick your teeth with.
他说，看，这根够直，正好可以用来剔牙。

1165
00:50:43.380 --> 00:50:44.940
He's, like, handing it to Nellie.
他当时好像正把它递给奈莉。

1166
00:50:45.040 --> 00:50:46.380
It's so disgusting.
太恶心了。

1167
00:50:46.940 --> 00:50:48.160
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1168
00:50:48.300 --> 00:50:51.520
This is our second cherry stem reference on The Office.
这是我们在《办公室》里第二次提到樱桃梗了。

1169
00:50:51.520 --> 00:50:52.640
Remember Ben Franklin?
还记得本·富兰克林吗？

1170
00:50:52.640 --> 00:50:53.880
Oh, yeah.
哦，记得。

1171
00:50:54.380 --> 00:50:54.600
Was.
是啊。

1172
00:50:54.780 --> 00:50:55.260
Was.
是啊。

1173
00:50:55.600 --> 00:50:55.660
Was.
是啊。

1174
00:50:55.660 --> 00:50:56.420
Cherry stem.
樱桃梗。

1175
00:50:56.700 --> 00:50:58.180
Was an expert with the cherry stem.
他可是樱桃梗专家。

1176
00:50:58.920 --> 00:51:04.320
Well, also in Tallahassee, Erin and Ryan have sneaked into the hotel kitchen to make a waffle.
另外在塔拉哈西，艾琳和瑞安溜进了酒店厨房去烤华夫饼。

1177
00:51:05.040 --> 00:51:09.520
And I'll have you know that we shot these kitchen scenes in the actual hotel kitchens.
我得告诉你们，这些厨房场景是我们实地在酒店厨房里拍摄的。

1178
00:51:09.880 --> 00:51:10.940
It looked real.
看起来很真实。

1179
00:51:11.180 --> 00:51:11.460
Yes.
是的。

1180
00:51:11.700 --> 00:51:13.680
In the morning, we took over the hotel bar.
早上我们占用了酒店酒吧。

1181
00:51:13.840 --> 00:51:15.600
And in the afternoon, we took over the kitchen.
下午我们占用了厨房。

1182
00:51:16.380 --> 00:51:21.080
And, you know, I'm always fascinated by the inner workings of the production.
你知道，我一直对制作过程的内部运作很着迷。

1183
00:51:21.280 --> 00:51:22.340
Like, how does this work?
比如，这是怎么运作的？

1184
00:51:22.480 --> 00:51:23.920
And I asked Steve Burgess.
我问了史蒂夫·伯吉斯。

1185
00:51:24.060 --> 00:51:28.440
And he said, you know, we shot at this hotel over two different weeks for two different episodes.
他说，我们在这家酒店分两周拍摄了两个不同的剧集。

1186
00:51:29.120 --> 00:51:31.360
He said it was like a whole ordeal.
他说这简直是一场大工程。

1187
00:51:31.600 --> 00:51:33.520
Like, we took over their parking lot.
比如，我们占用了他们的停车场。

1188
00:51:33.620 --> 00:51:35.620
We took over the whole second floor of the hotel.
我们占用了酒店的整个二楼。

1189
00:51:35.840 --> 00:51:39.180
On various days, we were in the lobby or the bar or the kitchen.
在不同的日子里，我们分别在大堂、酒吧或厨房拍摄。

1190
00:51:39.580 --> 00:51:41.420
During the week, we kept all our stuff there.
工作日期间，我们把所有东西都存放在那里。

1191
00:51:41.420 --> 00:51:44.480
They had guards that would guard everything like 24 hours a day.
他们安排了保安，24小时全天候看守所有东西。

1192
00:51:44.600 --> 00:51:47.720
But we would move it all back to our stages for the weekend.
但到了周末，我们又会把所有东西搬回摄影棚。

1193
00:51:48.240 --> 00:51:50.380
Because it wasn't just the stuff in the hotel either.
因为不仅仅是酒店里的那些东西。

1194
00:51:50.560 --> 00:51:53.460
Like, in the parking lot were all the crew trucks and all the trailers.
比如，停车场里停满了剧组的卡车和拖车。

1195
00:51:53.460 --> 00:51:58.180
And where we would eat lunch, you know, that was like where you would have catering for lunch.
还有我们吃午饭的地方，你知道，那是我们安排餐饮的地方。

1196
00:51:58.280 --> 00:51:59.280
It's like a whole thing.
这真的是一件大事。

1197
00:51:59.600 --> 00:52:01.660
Logistically, that is so much work.
从后勤角度看，工作量太大了。

1198
00:52:01.780 --> 00:52:06.020
Like, it's like every week you completely move into your house and then you move out.
就像每周都要彻底搬进一个房子，然后又搬出来一样。

1199
00:52:06.240 --> 00:52:06.520
Yes.
没错。

1200
00:52:06.640 --> 00:52:07.360
Imagine that.
想象一下吧。

1201
00:52:07.540 --> 00:52:07.840
Yes.
是的。

1202
00:52:08.180 --> 00:52:08.580
Exactly.
没错。

1203
00:52:09.100 --> 00:52:11.040
People working around the clock to make that happen.
人们夜以继日地工作，就是为了实现这一点。

1204
00:52:11.420 --> 00:52:12.140
Just amazing.
简直太棒了。

1205
00:52:12.520 --> 00:52:17.080
So also in this scene, Aaron says, oh, wow, they left the lights on.
在这一幕里，亚伦说，哇，他们居然没关灯。

1206
00:52:17.200 --> 00:52:21.580
And Ryan says that they leave the lights on because it's less expensive than turning them on and off.
瑞安说他们不关灯是因为这样比开关灯更省钱。

1207
00:52:21.720 --> 00:52:24.800
And Aaron is really impressed with how smart he is.
亚伦对他的聪明才智感到非常佩服。

1208
00:52:24.940 --> 00:52:25.120
Yeah.
是啊。

1209
00:52:25.500 --> 00:52:25.800
You know.
你知道的。

1210
00:52:26.420 --> 00:52:28.180
Well, I decided to check this out.
嗯，我决定去查证一下。

1211
00:52:28.420 --> 00:52:29.840
I wanted to fact check Ryan.
我想核实一下瑞安说的是不是真的。

1212
00:52:30.080 --> 00:52:30.720
Is this true?
这是真的吗？

1213
00:52:30.720 --> 00:52:36.960
Because, you know, sometimes you drive through a city late at night and you see these big, tall business buildings.
因为，你知道，有时候你深夜开车经过城市，会看到那些高大的商务楼。

1214
00:52:37.540 --> 00:52:42.400
And you know no one's in them, really, because it's nighttime and all the lights are on.
你知道里面其实根本没人，因为已经是深夜了，但灯却全亮着。

1215
00:52:42.400 --> 00:52:53.480
Well, according to energy.gov, the cost effectiveness of when to turn the lights on or off depends on the kind of bulb and the cost of electricity.
根据能源部官网（energy.gov）的说法，何时开关灯的成本效益取决于灯泡的类型和电费。

1216
00:52:53.480 --> 00:52:57.280
So light bulbs have a kind of operating life.
灯泡都有一定的使用寿命。

1217
00:52:57.420 --> 00:53:01.140
And that can be affected by how many times they're turned on and off.
而这会受到开关次数的影响。

1218
00:53:01.280 --> 00:53:05.360
So the more often they're switched on and off, the lower their operating life.
所以开关次数越频繁，它们的使用寿命就越短。

1219
00:53:05.560 --> 00:53:07.720
But I can get more specific with you.
我可以跟你说得更具体一点。

1220
00:53:08.600 --> 00:53:15.220
Incandescent lighting should definitely be turned off if you're not using it because they're the least efficient kind of lighting.
白炽灯如果不用的话绝对应该关掉，因为它们是效率最低的照明方式。

1221
00:53:15.220 --> 00:53:16.580
They give off a lot of heat.
它们会散发大量热量。

1222
00:53:16.740 --> 00:53:19.400
You'll keep your room cooler by turning them off.
关掉它们能让你的房间更凉快。

1223
00:53:19.540 --> 00:53:21.580
And you'll use less electricity.
而且还能节省用电。

1224
00:53:22.300 --> 00:53:26.860
Halogen lighting is slightly more efficient but should also be turned off when not in use.
卤素灯的效率稍高一些，但不用时也应该关掉。

1225
00:53:27.880 --> 00:53:34.720
However, fluorescent lighting is the light where you shorten the light span if you turn it on and off.
不过，荧光灯如果频繁开关，确实会缩短其使用寿命。

1226
00:53:35.020 --> 00:53:40.400
And there's a popular belief that these lights use a lot of energy to get started, which is true.
人们普遍认为这些灯启动时非常耗电，这确实是真的。

1227
00:53:40.420 --> 00:53:42.340
You know, when you turn on fluorescent lights, it's like.
你知道，当你打开荧光灯时，就像是。

1228
00:53:43.780 --> 00:53:44.280
Yeah.
是啊。

1229
00:53:44.280 --> 00:53:48.600
And it is better to not turn them off for short periods of time.
短时间内不关灯确实更好。

1230
00:53:48.940 --> 00:53:51.740
But you could turn them off for like all night.
但如果是整晚不用，你完全可以关掉。

1231
00:53:51.960 --> 00:53:57.400
But if you're just leaving this hotel kitchen for like 30 minutes, just leave them on.
但如果你只是离开酒店厨房半小时左右，那就让它亮着吧。

1232
00:53:57.820 --> 00:54:04.680
In short, it's not about the cost of electricity that you save, but on the replacement coSt.
简而言之，这省下的不是电费，而是更换灯管的成本。

1233
00:54:04.900 --> 00:54:07.520
Like you'd have to replace those fluorescent lights more often.
也就是说，你得更频繁地更换那些荧光灯。

1234
00:54:07.760 --> 00:54:10.280
So I guess Ryan's right.
所以我猜瑞安是对的。

1235
00:54:10.540 --> 00:54:14.120
Because then your carbon footprint is building more lights.
因为这样的话，你的碳足迹就包括了制造更多灯管。

1236
00:54:14.700 --> 00:54:15.960
Using more materials.
消耗更多材料。

1237
00:54:16.280 --> 00:54:18.300
Using the machinery to make the lights.
使用制造灯管的机器。

1238
00:54:18.960 --> 00:54:23.280
And the cost of having to buy all the light bulbs and the labor of putting them in.
还有购买所有灯泡的成本以及安装它们的人工费。

1239
00:54:23.560 --> 00:54:23.780
Yeah.
是啊。

1240
00:54:24.180 --> 00:54:25.600
So I guess Ryan's right.
所以我猜瑞安是对的。

1241
00:54:25.600 --> 00:54:26.240
I was annoyed.
我当时很恼火。

1242
00:54:26.380 --> 00:54:27.340
I wanted Ryan to be wrong.
我本来希望瑞安是错的。

1243
00:54:28.120 --> 00:54:30.980
Ryan is working so hard to get laid.
瑞安为了泡妞真是太拼了。

1244
00:54:31.160 --> 00:54:31.920
My gosh.
天哪。

1245
00:54:32.740 --> 00:54:34.020
He's really working hard.
他真的很努力。

1246
00:54:34.780 --> 00:54:35.820
It made me cringe.
看得我尴尬症都犯了。

1247
00:54:36.080 --> 00:54:36.960
It did me too.
我也是。

1248
00:54:40.690 --> 00:54:43.770
So listen, all of a sudden though, people are going to come in this kitchen.
听着，突然之间，有人要进这个厨房了。

1249
00:54:44.190 --> 00:54:50.090
And I guess what they decide to do, rather than just act like, oh my gosh, sorry, we didn't mean to be in here.
我猜他们决定怎么做呢，而不是表现得像，噢天哪，抱歉，我们不是故意要进来的。

1250
00:54:50.090 --> 00:54:54.370
We got turned around, which is what I would do if I was caught sneaking into a kitchen.
我们走错路了，如果是我被抓到溜进厨房，我肯定会这么说。

1251
00:54:55.470 --> 00:55:02.270
They decide to hide in the kitchen, a la Jurassic Park, kind of like under the table.
他们决定躲在厨房里，就像《侏罗纪公园》里那样，差不多是躲在桌子底下。

1252
00:55:02.710 --> 00:55:03.450
From the raptors.
躲避迅猛龙。

1253
00:55:03.570 --> 00:55:04.750
Yeah, that's what it reminded me of.
对，我就是想到了那个场景。

1254
00:55:04.970 --> 00:55:10.270
You know what's a great thing to do if you're somewhere and you maybe shouldn't be in that part of a building?
你知道如果你身处某栋建筑里不该去的地方，最好的应对办法是什么吗？

1255
00:55:10.410 --> 00:55:10.990
Okay, what?
好，是什么？

1256
00:55:11.190 --> 00:55:12.130
If you're discovered.
如果你被发现了的话。

1257
00:55:12.430 --> 00:55:12.730
What?
什么？

1258
00:55:13.310 --> 00:55:14.630
Just say, bathroom?
就说，洗手间在哪？

1259
00:55:14.990 --> 00:55:17.610
Why do we have so many excuses?
为什么我们有这么多借口？

1260
00:55:17.950 --> 00:55:25.130
Why are we so ready to get out of a situation where we're in a part of a building we shouldn't be in?
为什么我们总是随时准备好从不该待的地方脱身？

1261
00:55:25.170 --> 00:55:26.790
Have we done this a lot in our life?
我们生活中经常干这种事吗？

1262
00:55:26.890 --> 00:55:27.130
Why?
为什么？

1263
00:55:27.350 --> 00:55:30.050
I think we're both like snoops.
我觉得我们俩都有点爱打探。

1264
00:55:30.250 --> 00:55:33.170
And we're like, we're both like, oh, oh, it's the kitchen.
我们俩会说，噢，噢，那是厨房。

1265
00:55:33.270 --> 00:55:33.710
Oh, no one's in.
噢，没人。

1266
00:55:33.770 --> 00:55:34.330
Let's go look.
我们去看看吧。

1267
00:55:34.410 --> 00:55:35.090
Let's see what's in there.
看看里面有什么。

1268
00:55:35.550 --> 00:55:36.630
It's very innocent.
这很单纯。

1269
00:55:36.630 --> 00:55:38.810
But I think you and I both snoop a little bit.
但我认为你和我都有点爱打探。

1270
00:55:39.030 --> 00:55:40.190
I think you're right.
我想你是对的。

1271
00:55:40.410 --> 00:55:42.010
So we have it on the ready.
所以我们随时准备着。

1272
00:55:42.010 --> 00:55:42.810
Why are we?
为什么我们会这样？

1273
00:55:43.090 --> 00:55:43.150
Yeah.
是啊。

1274
00:55:43.190 --> 00:55:44.730
Oh, I'm so sorry.
噢，真抱歉。

1275
00:55:44.830 --> 00:55:45.530
I got turned around.
我迷路了。

1276
00:55:45.710 --> 00:55:45.870
I'm sorry.
对不起。

1277
00:55:45.990 --> 00:55:46.410
Bathroom?
洗手间在哪？

1278
00:55:48.920 --> 00:55:51.340
On the next episode of Mom Detectives.
在下一集《妈妈侦探》中。

1279
00:55:51.520 --> 00:55:55.120
Well, we're going to use both those excuses in an upcoming snoop.
好吧，我们下次打探时会用上这两个借口。

1280
00:55:55.660 --> 00:55:57.160
Let's go back to Jim's room.
让我们回到吉姆的房间。

1281
00:55:57.680 --> 00:55:58.860
There's a knock at the door.
有人敲门。

1282
00:55:59.400 --> 00:56:00.240
It's Stanley.
是斯坦利。

1283
00:56:00.560 --> 00:56:01.600
Oh, Jim's so relieved.
噢，吉姆如释重负。

1284
00:56:01.760 --> 00:56:01.980
Yes.
是的。

1285
00:56:02.080 --> 00:56:02.500
Come in.
进来。

1286
00:56:02.640 --> 00:56:02.720
Come in.
进来。

1287
00:56:02.720 --> 00:56:03.700
Watch the game with us.
和我们一起看比赛吧。

1288
00:56:03.840 --> 00:56:04.060
Yes.
好。

1289
00:56:04.440 --> 00:56:05.740
Stanley just wants some rum.
斯坦利只是想喝点朗姆酒。

1290
00:56:05.900 --> 00:56:08.680
For some reason, his mini fridge is out of rum.
不知为何，他的迷你冰箱里没酒了。

1291
00:56:08.840 --> 00:56:09.600
I wonder why.
我好奇为什么。

1292
00:56:09.740 --> 00:56:10.140
I wonder.
我也好奇。

1293
00:56:10.320 --> 00:56:11.040
Florida Stanley.
佛罗里达的斯坦利。

1294
00:56:12.220 --> 00:56:15.060
And Stanley clocks that Kathy's on the bed.
斯坦利注意到了凯西在床上。

1295
00:56:15.120 --> 00:56:17.660
And he's like, oh, it gets easier and easier, Jim.
他说，噢，吉姆，这真是越来越容易了。

1296
00:56:18.060 --> 00:56:18.580
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1297
00:56:18.860 --> 00:56:20.920
And Jim's like, no, that's not what's.
吉姆说，不，不是那样的。

1298
00:56:20.920 --> 00:56:21.760
And he's like, whatever.
他说，随便吧。

1299
00:56:21.760 --> 00:56:22.740
And he leaves.
然后他就走了。

1300
00:56:23.380 --> 00:56:26.420
So Jim is going to have to enlist Dwight.
所以吉姆不得不求助德怀特了。

1301
00:56:26.780 --> 00:56:27.040
Yeah.
是啊。

1302
00:56:27.160 --> 00:56:29.960
He's come up with a plan of how to get Kathy out of his room.
他想出了一个把凯西赶出他房间的计划。

1303
00:56:30.460 --> 00:56:33.100
Because I guess he's too nice to just ask her to leave.
因为我觉得他太好心了，不好意思直接让她走。

1304
00:56:33.680 --> 00:56:35.100
That's my bullshit card.
那是我的胡扯牌。

1305
00:56:35.280 --> 00:56:35.640
I know.
我知道。

1306
00:56:35.640 --> 00:56:37.180
Just ask her to leave.
直接让她走就行了。

1307
00:56:37.480 --> 00:56:38.540
Say, I'm tired.
就说，我累了。

1308
00:56:38.540 --> 00:56:39.660
I need you to go.
我需要你离开。

1309
00:56:39.920 --> 00:56:41.200
I need to go to bed.
我得去睡觉了。

1310
00:56:41.380 --> 00:56:41.700
Yeah.
是啊。

1311
00:56:41.920 --> 00:56:44.920
I actually need to call Pam and catch up with a few things.
我其实得给帕姆打个电话，处理一些事情。

1312
00:56:45.100 --> 00:56:45.420
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1313
00:56:45.620 --> 00:56:47.240
I'm going to ask you to go.
我要请你离开了。

1314
00:56:47.460 --> 00:56:48.340
Have a good night.
晚安。

1315
00:56:48.560 --> 00:56:50.700
I've got a fan mail flurry on this subject.
关于这个话题，我收到了一大堆粉丝来信。

1316
00:56:50.780 --> 00:56:50.940
All right.
好吧。

1317
00:56:51.060 --> 00:56:51.860
Coming up, lady.
来了，女士。

1318
00:56:52.060 --> 00:56:54.460
My bullshit card, I had to play one.
我的胡扯牌，我不得不打出一张。

1319
00:56:54.640 --> 00:57:01.320
So Jim finds Dwight, interrupts his seduction plan to tell him there are bed bugs in his room.
所以吉姆找到了德怀特，打断了他的诱惑计划，告诉他房间里有臭虫。

1320
00:57:01.540 --> 00:57:02.100
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1321
00:57:02.100 --> 00:57:04.980
Because talk about playing the player.
因为这简直是高手过招。

1322
00:57:05.380 --> 00:57:06.920
This is going to freak Dwight out.
这会把德怀特吓坏的。

1323
00:57:07.140 --> 00:57:07.660
Bed bugs.
臭虫。

1324
00:57:07.860 --> 00:57:08.820
He'll be right there.
他马上就会过去。

1325
00:57:08.980 --> 00:57:09.240
Yeah.
是啊。

1326
00:57:09.740 --> 00:57:13.200
But then Dwight's like, oh, I don't want Packer to hook up with Nellie.
但后来德怀特心想，哦，我不想让帕克和内莉搞在一起。

1327
00:57:13.460 --> 00:57:19.500
So he goes up to Gabe and says, I need you to help me sabotage this.
于是他去找盖博说，我需要你帮我搞破坏。

1328
00:57:20.160 --> 00:57:20.300
Yeah.
是啊。

1329
00:57:20.820 --> 00:57:22.980
This is when we find out Gabe's full name.
就在这时我们知道了盖博的全名。

1330
00:57:23.640 --> 00:57:24.940
Gabriel Susan Lewis.
加布里埃尔·苏珊·刘易斯。

1331
00:57:25.460 --> 00:57:25.900
GSL.
GSL。

1332
00:57:26.040 --> 00:57:27.360
What's in it for GSL?
这对GSL有什么好处？

1333
00:57:27.620 --> 00:57:29.560
I loved what's in it for GSL.
我喜欢那句“这对GSL有什么好处”。

1334
00:57:29.580 --> 00:57:31.620
Dwight's like, do you really want Packer as a boss?
德怀特说，你真的想让帕克当你的老板吗？

1335
00:57:31.620 --> 00:57:32.840
That's all he needed to hear.
他只需要听到这些就够了。

1336
00:57:33.020 --> 00:57:33.280
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1337
00:57:33.880 --> 00:57:39.740
Dwight is going to burst into Jim's room, forces Kathy off the bed so that he can shake
德怀特冲进吉姆的房间，强行把凯西从床上拉下来，这样他就能抖掉

1338
00:57:39.740 --> 00:57:42.560
out all the covers and find the bed bugs.
所有的被子，找出臭虫。

1339
00:57:43.060 --> 00:57:45.500
Then Dwight starts interrogating Jim.
然后德怀特开始审问吉姆。

1340
00:57:45.700 --> 00:57:50.300
He's searching his hair and asking him a whole bunch of questions about his encounter with
他搜查他的头发，问了他一大堆关于他遇到

1341
00:57:50.300 --> 00:57:50.900
the bed bug.
臭虫的问题。

1342
00:57:51.320 --> 00:57:52.960
Dwight says, where did you see it?
德怀特问，你在哪儿看到的？

1343
00:57:53.080 --> 00:57:54.280
Jim says, in the bed.
吉姆说，在床上。

1344
00:57:54.680 --> 00:57:56.540
Dwight's like, we got to find it before it eggs.
德怀特说，我们必须在它产卵前找到它。

1345
00:57:57.240 --> 00:57:58.020
Describe it.
描述一下它。

1346
00:57:58.260 --> 00:58:01.000
Jim says, brown, shiny, painful bite.
吉姆说，棕色，有光泽，咬人很疼。

1347
00:58:01.000 --> 00:58:03.260
Dwight, hmm, could be a bat weevil.
德怀特说，嗯，可能是蝙蝠象鼻虫。

1348
00:58:03.360 --> 00:58:04.080
Describe its mood.
描述一下它的情绪。

1349
00:58:04.300 --> 00:58:05.460
Did it seem sleepy?
它看起来困吗？

1350
00:58:06.000 --> 00:58:07.420
Jim, stressed.
吉姆说，压力很大。

1351
00:58:07.600 --> 00:58:09.620
But to be fair, it was a tense situation.
但平心而论，当时情况确实很紧张。

1352
00:58:09.880 --> 00:58:10.900
Dwight, fair enough.
德怀特，说得有道理。

1353
00:58:11.060 --> 00:58:16.420
But after it bit you, did it run away fearful or did it walk away smug, self-assured?
但它咬了你之后，是惊慌失措地跑开了，还是洋洋得意、自信满满地走开了？

1354
00:58:16.840 --> 00:58:18.660
Jim, so smug.
吉姆，特别得意。

1355
00:58:18.780 --> 00:58:20.840
Like he thought it was funny, like this.
就像他觉得这很好笑，就像这样。

1356
00:58:21.320 --> 00:58:23.880
And then Dwight's like, that's a bed bug.
然后德怀特说，那是只臭虫。

1357
00:58:24.120 --> 00:58:25.060
Everything's a joke.
什么事都能当笑话。

1358
00:58:25.060 --> 00:58:32.660
Lady, so I told you, I was at this location and I arrived and they were getting ready to
女士，我跟你说过了，我当时在那儿，我刚到，他们正准备

1359
00:58:32.660 --> 00:58:33.700
shoot this scene.
拍这场戏。

1360
00:58:34.000 --> 00:58:36.120
It was so funny.
太搞笑了。

1361
00:58:36.320 --> 00:58:42.220
The first time John imitated the smug bed bug, it was the same as the unbelievable scene.
约翰第一次模仿那只得意的臭虫时，和那场不可思议的戏一模一样。

1362
00:58:42.400 --> 00:58:49.860
Like Rain was like shocked at how funny it was and he started laughing and they could not
雷恩当时被逗得目瞪口呆，他开始大笑，他们根本

1363
00:58:49.860 --> 00:58:50.620
get through it.
拍不下去。

1364
00:58:50.760 --> 00:58:56.700
Like every time John imitated the smug bed bug, oh my God, it was amazing.
每次约翰模仿那只得意的臭虫，天哪，简直绝了。

1365
00:58:56.800 --> 00:59:01.120
I was sitting with Brian at the director's monitor and I remember coming into work the
我当时和布莱恩坐在导演监视器旁，我记得第二天来到片场时，

1366
00:59:01.120 --> 00:59:06.800
next day on our stages and I was trying to like recreate it for everyone.
我试着向大家重现那一幕。

1367
00:59:06.900 --> 00:59:09.900
I was trying to explain, like you guys, you don't understand.
我试图解释，我说你们不懂。

1368
00:59:09.900 --> 00:59:14.240
It was like 30 minutes of trying to get John to imitate a smug bed bug because we're laughing
我们花了大概30分钟想让约翰模仿那只得意的臭虫，因为我们笑得

1369
00:59:14.240 --> 00:59:15.680
so hard and nobody got it.
太厉害了，没人能接得上话。

1370
00:59:15.740 --> 00:59:16.600
It was like crickets.
现场一片死寂。

1371
00:59:16.600 --> 00:59:19.900
I was like, just wait till this episode comes out.
我说，等着看这集播出吧。

1372
00:59:20.260 --> 00:59:25.600
I remember at the end of our season wrap party, they put the bloopers from it.
我记得在季终杀青派对上，他们放了花絮片段。

1373
00:59:25.780 --> 00:59:26.080
Yes.
没错。

1374
00:59:26.300 --> 00:59:29.660
There were so many and we were dying.
花絮特别多，我们当时都快笑死了。

1375
00:59:29.680 --> 00:59:31.080
We were dying.
我们都快笑死了。

1376
00:59:31.080 --> 00:59:32.360
It was so hilarious.
太搞笑了。

1377
00:59:32.600 --> 00:59:39.240
I was so happy they did that because I finally felt like everyone could see and share in this
我很高兴他们这么做，因为我终于觉得大家都能看到并分享这个

1378
00:59:39.240 --> 00:59:42.440
moment that is like one of the hardest we ever laughed on the set.
时刻了，这绝对是我们片场笑得最厉害的时刻之一。

1379
00:59:42.600 --> 00:59:46.420
That was always one of my favorite things of the wrap party because, you know,
那一直是我在杀青派对上最喜欢的部分，因为，你知道的，

1380
00:59:46.420 --> 00:59:48.280
there are a few bloopers that live out there.
外面流传的花絮也就那么几个。

1381
00:59:48.500 --> 00:59:50.600
You can find them on YouTube and places like that.
你可以在YouTube之类的地方找到它们。

1382
00:59:50.740 --> 00:59:55.600
But our editors would make a huge extended bloopers cut for the wrap party.
但我们的剪辑师会为杀青派对制作一个超长的花絮剪辑版。

1383
00:59:56.020 --> 00:59:56.960
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

1384
00:59:57.100 --> 00:59:59.060
I don't know how they ever got one take of that.
我不知道他们是怎么拍出一条能用的镜头的。

1385
00:59:59.260 --> 01:00:00.420
It was so good.
太棒了。

1386
01:00:00.600 --> 01:00:03.980
There are so many moments between Jim and Dwight in this hotel room.
吉姆和德怀特在酒店房间里有太多精彩瞬间了。

1387
01:00:04.080 --> 01:00:08.740
Like when Dwight says that he farted constantly under the sheet to make a greenhouse.
比如德怀特说他在被子里不断放屁来制造温室效应。

1388
01:00:08.840 --> 01:00:10.520
Like how did they get through any of it?
他们到底是怎么拍完这些戏的？

1389
01:00:10.520 --> 01:00:11.640
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

1390
01:00:12.080 --> 01:00:15.620
Well, Dwight is going to now remove all of his clothing.
好吧，德怀特现在要脱掉他所有的衣服。

1391
01:00:15.840 --> 01:00:19.580
Like you said, he's going to get into the bed under the covers.
就像你说的，他要钻进被子里。

1392
01:00:19.840 --> 01:00:22.160
He's going to attract the bed bugs with the body heat.
他要用体温吸引臭虫。

1393
01:00:22.340 --> 01:00:23.260
Yes, exactly.
没错，正是这样。

1394
01:00:23.580 --> 01:00:25.540
Also, when he went through Jim's hair.
还有，当他翻弄吉姆头发的时候。

1395
01:00:25.880 --> 01:00:26.220
Yes.
没错。

1396
01:00:26.220 --> 01:00:27.040
Come on.
得了吧。

1397
01:00:27.740 --> 01:00:29.440
Well, Kathy is so disgusted.
凯西觉得太恶心了。

1398
01:00:29.600 --> 01:00:31.100
She's like, I need to take a shower.
她说，我得去洗个澡。

1399
01:00:31.300 --> 01:00:32.540
And Jim's like, yes.
吉姆说，好的。

1400
01:00:32.720 --> 01:00:33.060
Bye-bye.
拜拜。

1401
01:00:33.080 --> 01:00:33.480
She's leaving.
她要走了。

1402
01:00:33.760 --> 01:00:36.000
And then she goes into his bathroom.
然后她进了他的浴室。

1403
01:00:36.180 --> 01:00:36.800
I am sorry.
我很抱歉。

1404
01:00:37.240 --> 01:00:38.280
Second bullshit card.
第二张胡扯牌。

1405
01:00:38.280 --> 01:00:40.140
Who does that?
谁会那样做？

1406
01:00:40.400 --> 01:00:41.360
Who does that?
谁会那样做？

1407
01:00:41.640 --> 01:00:44.300
I do have a third bull**** card to play.
我确实还有第三张胡扯牌要出。

1408
01:00:44.540 --> 01:00:47.120
How is Dwight jumping into a bed?
德怀特是怎么跳到床上的？

1409
01:00:47.420 --> 01:00:50.360
He had his appendix out just the week before.
他就在一周前才刚切除阑尾。

1410
01:00:50.780 --> 01:00:52.620
How is he doing any of this?
他怎么能做这些动作的？

1411
01:00:53.140 --> 01:00:53.740
Angela.
安吉拉。

1412
01:00:54.040 --> 01:00:57.560
This was a fan catch from Angela B in New Hampshire.
这是来自新罕布什尔州的安吉拉·B的粉丝提问。

