You can get men's bootcut cords.
你可以买到男士微喇灯芯绒裤。

1567
01:07:30.520 --> 01:07:34.560
In fact, they were labeled as being back in style.
事实上，它们被贴上了回归潮流的标签。

1568
01:07:35.180 --> 01:07:41.040
You can find them at Walmart for $36.99, and they come in a variety of colors.
你可以在沃尔玛以36.99美元的价格买到，而且颜色多样。

1569
01:07:41.420 --> 01:07:47.980
You can get black, coffee, khaki, wine red, or cream white.
有黑色、咖啡色、卡其色、酒红色或奶油白色。

1570
01:07:48.280 --> 01:07:49.880
Give them to me in cream white.
给我来条奶油白色的。

1571
01:07:50.280 --> 01:07:51.040
I'm just kidding.
我开玩笑的。

1572
01:07:51.240 --> 01:07:51.560
I'm kidding.
我开玩笑呢。

1573
01:07:51.740 --> 01:07:55.960
I saw the picture of just these white bootcut cords, and I wondered,
我看到这些白色微喇裤的照片时，就在想，

1574
01:07:55.960 --> 01:07:58.940
where are we going to go in these?
穿着这裤子我们能去哪儿呢？

1575
01:07:59.120 --> 01:07:59.440
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1576
01:08:00.120 --> 01:08:01.140
But yes, they're available.
不过是的，它们确实有卖。

1577
01:08:01.720 --> 01:08:06.360
Speaking of Tala Nasty, somebody's going to get hashtag Tala Nasty'd.
说到“塔拉·纳斯蒂”，有人要被“塔拉·纳斯蒂”标签化了。

1578
01:08:06.820 --> 01:08:08.240
And so it begins.
好戏开场了。

1579
01:08:08.600 --> 01:08:08.860
Yeah.
是啊。

1580
01:08:09.140 --> 01:08:10.000
Buckle in, everyone.
大家系好安全带。

1581
01:08:10.280 --> 01:08:14.500
Buckle in, because Kathy is going to order room service, and then she's like,
系好安全带，因为凯西要点客房服务了，然后她会说，

1582
01:08:14.620 --> 01:08:17.160
oh, but, you know, I work out.
噢，但是，你知道，我有健身。

1583
01:08:17.380 --> 01:08:18.240
Fill my legs.
摸摸我的腿。

1584
01:08:18.460 --> 01:08:19.740
Fill my leg?
摸你的腿？

1585
01:08:19.940 --> 01:08:20.140
Yeah.
对。

1586
01:08:20.300 --> 01:08:22.920
By the way, she's been putting lotion on in front of him.
顺便说一句，她一直在他面前涂润肤露。

1587
01:08:22.980 --> 01:08:23.640
I mean, what?
我是说，搞什么？

1588
01:08:23.640 --> 01:08:24.540
Stop it, Kathy.
别这样，凯西。

1589
01:08:24.780 --> 01:08:25.380
Stop it.
住手。

1590
01:08:25.380 --> 01:08:26.160
This is it.
就是现在。

1591
01:08:26.280 --> 01:08:28.880
Jim is like, okay, listen, I think I just need to say it.
吉姆心想，好吧，听着，我觉得我必须得说出来。

1592
01:08:29.140 --> 01:08:30.080
I am married.
我结婚了。

1593
01:08:30.200 --> 01:08:31.620
I'm actually very happily married.
而且我的婚姻非常幸福。

1594
01:08:31.800 --> 01:08:34.680
And then she does such a bitchy thing.
然后她做了一件特别刻薄的事。

1595
01:08:34.780 --> 01:08:35.080
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1596
01:08:35.260 --> 01:08:38.700
She goes, I'm sorry, what are you talking about?
她说，抱歉，你在说什么呢？

1597
01:08:40.740 --> 01:08:43.580
I sat at your wife's desk.
我坐在你妻子的办公桌前。

1598
01:08:43.580 --> 01:08:45.480
I know you're married.
我知道你结婚了。

1599
01:08:46.020 --> 01:08:48.360
How little do you think of me?
你觉得我是那种人吗？

1600
01:08:48.800 --> 01:08:51.040
And then Jim is really thrown.
然后吉姆彻底懵了。

1601
01:08:51.060 --> 01:08:54.600
He's like, I'm sorry, I guess I read this wrong.
他当时就像是，抱歉，我想我读错了。

1602
01:08:54.980 --> 01:08:57.200
And now he's going against all of his instincts.
现在他要违背自己所有的直觉了。

1603
01:08:57.640 --> 01:08:58.000
Yeah.
是啊。

1604
01:08:58.280 --> 01:08:58.520
Right?
对吧？

1605
01:08:58.700 --> 01:08:59.500
He's like, you know what?
他当时就像是，你知道吗？

1606
01:08:59.600 --> 01:08:59.880
Fine.
好吧。

1607
01:09:00.080 --> 01:09:00.680
You can stay.
你可以留下。

1608
01:09:00.860 --> 01:09:04.660
And then she's like, you promise you won't run to the other side of the room all night?
然后她就说，你保证今晚不会跑到房间的另一边去吗？

1609
01:09:04.660 --> 01:09:06.920
He's like, yeah, sure, sure.
他就像是，行，没问题，没问题。

1610
01:09:07.060 --> 01:09:08.100
We'll just watch the game.
我们就只是看比赛。

1611
01:09:08.460 --> 01:09:11.600
And he sits down, and she snuggles up right next to him.
然后他坐下，她就紧紧依偎在他身边。

1612
01:09:11.600 --> 01:09:14.600
Here began the fan mail flurry.
粉丝来信狂潮就这样开始了。

1613
01:09:15.200 --> 01:09:16.180
Let's hear it.
让我们听听看。

1614
01:09:16.380 --> 01:09:19.720
It goes something like this I'm pulling from several letters.
内容大概是这样的，我综合了几封信的内容。

1615
01:09:20.180 --> 01:09:22.020
Quote, what the hell, Jim?
引用一下，搞什么鬼，吉姆？

1616
01:09:22.260 --> 01:09:22.620
Yeah.
没错。

1617
01:09:23.160 --> 01:09:25.540
You are to blame here, Jim.
吉姆，这事儿得怪你。

1618
01:09:25.820 --> 01:09:26.240
Uh-oh.
噢哦。

1619
01:09:26.560 --> 01:09:28.000
Stand up for something, man.
男人，拿出点立场来。

1620
01:09:28.180 --> 01:09:29.020
Put your foot down.
态度强硬点。

1621
01:09:29.220 --> 01:09:31.360
Get this woman out of your room.
让这个女人离开你的房间。

1622
01:09:31.520 --> 01:09:34.640
And if you can't, then leave the room yourself.
如果做不到，那你就自己离开房间。

1623
01:09:34.920 --> 01:09:36.160
And don't go back.
而且别再回去。

1624
01:09:36.160 --> 01:09:38.540
He went down to the bar to get right.
他去酒吧喝一杯想理清思绪。

1625
01:09:38.780 --> 01:09:39.860
Just stay at the bar.
就待在酒吧别回来了。

1626
01:09:40.180 --> 01:09:41.000
No kidding.
说真的。

1627
01:09:41.440 --> 01:09:45.200
I am reading it like this because there was a lot of all caps.
我之所以这样读，是因为信里用了大量大写字母。

1628
01:09:45.440 --> 01:09:45.820
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1629
01:09:45.860 --> 01:09:46.560
Just so you know.
让你知道一下。

1630
01:09:46.740 --> 01:09:47.440
There's more.
还有呢。

1631
01:09:47.800 --> 01:09:50.220
I cannot stand Jim in this episode.
这一集里我简直受不了吉姆。

1632
01:09:50.480 --> 01:09:53.600
Please, please discuss this at great length, ladies.
拜托，拜托，女士们，请详细讨论一下这个问题。

1633
01:09:54.320 --> 01:09:54.960
More mail.
更多来信。

1634
01:09:54.960 --> 01:10:01.680
Well, Kiana from Oregon said, I never understood how this whole Kathy situation was never discussed
嗯，来自俄勒冈州的基亚娜说，我一直不明白为什么凯西的整件事从来没有在屏幕上

1635
01:10:01.680 --> 01:10:03.460
on screen with Jim and Pam.
被吉姆和帕姆讨论过。

1636
01:10:03.680 --> 01:10:04.780
Did he ever tell her?
他有告诉过她吗？

1637
01:10:05.120 --> 01:10:10.160
And Morgan in Raleigh, North Carolina said, please tell me there's a deleted scene that
来自北卡罗来纳州罗利的摩根说，请告诉我有一个我们不知道的删减片段。

1638
01:10:10.160 --> 01:10:11.080
we don't know about.
噢，是的，确实有。

1639
01:10:11.600 --> 01:10:13.680
Oh, yes, there was.
确实有一个非常重要的片段。

1640
01:10:13.940 --> 01:10:15.900
There was a very big scene.
它被删掉了。

1641
01:10:16.080 --> 01:10:16.680
It was deleted.
它本应出现在帕姆和安迪走进达里尔办公室的下一场戏之后。

1642
01:10:16.900 --> 01:10:21.980
It would have come after the next scene when Pam and Andy go into Daryl's office.
是的，当时达里尔因为瓦尔的男朋友感到很沮丧。

1643
01:10:21.980 --> 01:10:25.020
Yes, so Daryl is bummed about Val's boyfriend.
嗯哼。

1644
01:10:25.240 --> 01:10:25.520
Uh-huh.
安迪和帕姆走进他的办公室。

1645
01:10:25.940 --> 01:10:27.280
Andy and Pam go into his office.
安迪说，冷静点。

1646
01:10:27.460 --> 01:10:28.860
Andy's saying, play it cool.
瓦尔会回心转意的。

1647
01:10:29.060 --> 01:10:29.980
Val will come around.
帕姆说，不，直接冲吧。

1648
01:10:30.160 --> 01:10:32.200
And Pam says, no, just go for it.
安迪说，不，吉姆会让你冷静点的。

1649
01:10:32.320 --> 01:10:36.100
And Andy says, no, Jim would tell you to play it cool.
帕姆说，吉姆会让你直接冲的。

1650
01:10:36.280 --> 01:10:39.680
And Pam says, Jim would tell you to go for it.
帕姆说，吉姆会让你直接冲的。

1651
01:10:39.840 --> 01:10:40.020
Yeah.
没错。

1652
01:10:40.180 --> 01:10:42.660
So now the scene would have extended.
所以现在的场景本该更长一些。

1653
01:10:42.980 --> 01:10:44.440
It's in deleted scenes.
它在删减片段里。

1654
01:10:44.440 --> 01:10:45.540
It would have continued.
它本该继续下去的。

1655
01:10:45.540 --> 01:10:47.800
And Pam would have said, well, you know what?
帕姆本该说，好吧，你知道吗？

1656
01:10:48.060 --> 01:10:49.660
Let's call Jim and ask him.
我们给吉姆打个电话问问他。

1657
01:10:49.660 --> 01:10:52.800
Basically, she's debating with Andy.
基本上，她在和安迪争论。

1658
01:10:53.060 --> 01:10:54.180
Is Andy right?
安迪是对的吗？

1659
01:10:54.320 --> 01:10:55.660
Is Jim going to say play it cool?
吉姆会说要冷静处理吗？

1660
01:10:55.800 --> 01:10:56.780
Or am I right?
还是我是对的？

1661
01:10:56.780 --> 01:10:57.580
I'm his wife.
我是他妻子。

1662
01:10:57.780 --> 01:10:58.120
Yes.
是的。

1663
01:10:58.220 --> 01:10:59.160
I think I know my husband.
我想我了解我丈夫。

1664
01:10:59.420 --> 01:11:06.000
So somehow by memory, she knows Jim's hotel room number in Tallahassee.
所以她凭记忆居然知道吉姆在塔拉哈西的酒店房间号。

1665
01:11:06.160 --> 01:11:07.780
And she puts this on speakerphone.
然后她开了免提。

1666
01:11:08.220 --> 01:11:10.220
And Kathy answers the phone.
凯西接了电话。

1667
01:11:10.620 --> 01:11:10.920
Yeah.
没错。

1668
01:11:11.380 --> 01:11:15.320
And Andy and Daryl and Pam are all like, huh.
安迪、达里尔和帕姆都一脸震惊。

1669
01:11:15.560 --> 01:11:16.760
So let's hear it.
那我们听听看吧。

1670
01:11:18.480 --> 01:11:19.960
Let's call Jim.
给吉姆打个电话。

1671
01:11:22.880 --> 01:11:23.880
You're going to be embarrassed.
你会感到尴尬的。

1672
01:11:24.100 --> 01:11:24.680
You think so?
你这么觉得？

1673
01:11:25.720 --> 01:11:26.200
Okay.
好吧。

1674
01:11:26.640 --> 01:11:27.320
We'll see.
走着瞧。

1675
01:11:27.860 --> 01:11:28.220
He'll tell you.
他会告诉你的。

1676
01:11:30.120 --> 01:11:30.900
Uh, hello?
呃，喂？

1677
01:11:31.100 --> 01:11:31.600
Who is this?
你是谁？

1678
01:11:37.860 --> 01:11:38.340
Hello.
喂。

1679
01:11:41.600 --> 01:11:42.080
Yeah.
嗯。

1680
01:11:42.600 --> 01:11:44.660
Yeah, I'm here with Andy and Daryl.
嗯，我和安迪还有达里尔在一起。

1681
01:11:44.900 --> 01:11:45.220
Do not.
别说。

1682
01:11:45.380 --> 01:11:46.680
What are you and Kathy up to?
你和凯西在干嘛呢？

1683
01:11:47.140 --> 01:11:48.040
Watching a game.
在看比赛。

1684
01:11:48.280 --> 01:11:49.120
Do you guys alone?
你们俩单独在一起吗？

1685
01:11:49.460 --> 01:11:51.100
Or did everyone come up from the bar?
还是大家都从酒吧上来了？

1686
01:11:51.400 --> 01:11:52.380
Just me and Kathy now.
现在只有我和凯西。

1687
01:11:58.580 --> 01:11:59.380
Don't do it.
别做那事。

1688
01:12:00.080 --> 01:12:01.020
Or do do it.
或者就做吧。

1689
01:12:01.340 --> 01:12:02.140
Whatever it is.
随你怎么做。

1690
01:12:02.240 --> 01:12:02.900
This is awesome.
这太棒了。

1691
01:12:03.640 --> 01:12:05.540
Uh, hey, babe, is Einstein with you?
呃，嘿，宝贝，爱因斯坦和你在一起吗？

1692
01:12:06.020 --> 01:12:06.420
No.
没有。

1693
01:12:09.350 --> 01:12:12.570
Einstein is the codename we use if we're ever caught in a home invasion scenario.
爱因斯坦是我们万一遇到入室抢劫时用的暗号。

1694
01:12:14.510 --> 01:12:15.970
As a parent, you think of these things.
作为父母，你总会考虑到这些。

1695
01:12:17.530 --> 01:12:19.550
Okay, so there's a lot of things happening here.
好吧，这里发生了很多事。

1696
01:12:19.750 --> 01:12:20.710
A lot of things to unpack.
有很多信息需要消化。

1697
01:12:21.230 --> 01:12:22.450
Pam is weirded out.
帕姆觉得很奇怪。

1698
01:12:22.870 --> 01:12:24.250
And like Kelly comes in.
然后凯莉进来了。

1699
01:12:24.390 --> 01:12:25.890
Kelly's having the best night of her life.
凯莉正度过她人生中最棒的一晚。

1700
01:12:25.990 --> 01:12:26.950
So much gossip.
好多八卦。

1701
01:12:26.950 --> 01:12:28.670
Yes, so much is happening.
没错，发生了太多事了。

1702
01:12:28.850 --> 01:12:30.530
It's the best night of her life, basically.
基本上，这是她人生中最棒的一晚。

1703
01:12:31.070 --> 01:12:35.390
Okay, so this kind of started something that never got resolved.
好吧，这件事引发了一些后续，但从未得到解决。

1704
01:12:35.630 --> 01:12:37.970
This was my complaint that I was talking about earlier,
这就是我刚才提到的那个抱怨，

1705
01:12:38.270 --> 01:12:41.610
which is that you were going to see Pam get insecure,
也就是说，你们会看到帕姆变得缺乏安全感，

1706
01:12:41.610 --> 01:12:47.150
and you were also going to see everyone in the office assume something was going on between Jim and Kathy.
而且你们还会看到办公室里的每个人都以为吉姆和凯西之间有什么。

1707
01:12:47.370 --> 01:12:47.630
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

1708
01:12:47.930 --> 01:12:48.750
Kelly's so excited.
凯莉太兴奋了。

1709
01:12:49.070 --> 01:12:52.410
And so because of that, John and I were like,
正因如此，我和约翰当时就觉得，

1710
01:12:52.510 --> 01:12:56.210
you have to write a scene that resolves this insecurity in Pam.
你们必须写一场戏来消除帕姆的这种不安全感。

1711
01:12:56.210 --> 01:12:57.210
Pam, you have to.
帕姆，你必须得写。

1712
01:12:57.850 --> 01:12:58.830
So they did.
于是他们照做了。

1713
01:12:58.830 --> 01:13:02.630
And then there was another scene that we shot that was also deleted.
然后我们还拍了另一场戏，后来也被删掉了。

1714
01:13:03.170 --> 01:13:04.550
Jim and Pam are on the phone.
吉姆和帕姆在通电话。

1715
01:13:04.730 --> 01:13:05.810
It would have played a little later.
那场戏本该在稍后播出。

1716
01:13:06.250 --> 01:13:07.150
Should we listen to that one?
我们要听听那段吗？

1717
01:13:07.250 --> 01:13:07.490
Yeah.
好啊。

1718
01:13:08.470 --> 01:13:10.030
She's still sitting right there.
她还坐在那儿呢。

1719
01:13:10.210 --> 01:13:11.810
You know she's lying about the heating.
你知道她在暖气的事上撒谎。

1720
01:13:12.250 --> 01:13:13.070
Of course.
当然。

1721
01:13:13.570 --> 01:13:14.590
I feel bad for her.
我为她感到难过。

1722
01:13:14.890 --> 01:13:15.990
It's really pathetic.
真的很可怜。

1723
01:13:16.850 --> 01:13:18.330
Yes, it is.
确实是。

1724
01:13:19.150 --> 01:13:20.850
I wish I was there to see your face.
真希望当时我在场，能看到你的表情。

1725
01:13:21.130 --> 01:13:23.110
You always look really cute when you're embarrassed.
你尴尬的时候看起来总是很可爱。

1726
01:13:23.950 --> 01:13:24.390
Okay.
好吧。

1727
01:13:24.810 --> 01:13:25.570
Ha, ha, ha.
哈哈哈哈。

1728
01:13:26.070 --> 01:13:26.790
I love you.
我爱你。

1729
01:13:26.890 --> 01:13:27.570
I'll talk to you later.
回头再聊。

1730
01:13:27.690 --> 01:13:28.410
Have fun with that.
祝你玩得开心。

1731
01:13:29.150 --> 01:13:29.990
Love you too.
我也爱你。

1732
01:13:30.450 --> 01:13:31.450
I will not.
我才不会玩得开心。

1733
01:13:35.420 --> 01:13:36.680
Nice to hear her voice.
听到她的声音真好。

1734
01:13:37.580 --> 01:13:39.420
Scranton building three miles away, right?
斯克兰顿大楼就在三英里外，对吧？

1735
01:13:41.160 --> 01:13:46.960
So the point of that one was to show that like Pam is on to Kathy, she is in no way insecure.
那场戏的重点是想表现帕姆已经看穿了凯西，她一点也不缺乏安全感。

1736
01:13:47.280 --> 01:13:47.620
Yeah.
没错。

1737
01:13:47.620 --> 01:13:50.200
And in fact is somewhat amused by Jim's predicament.
事实上，她甚至觉得吉姆的处境挺好笑的。

1738
01:13:50.440 --> 01:13:50.540
Yeah.
